{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>A spring</b> — [verses 26–27] two joined pericopes. <b>מעין ומקור</b> (a spring and a fountain) is a duplication, meaning: like a spring that the mud tramples and like a fountain of waters that is ruined, so the righteous man who totters before a wicked man — he likened him to a spring, for his mouth is a fountain of reproofs, and it is not fitting that the wicked should trample him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved המוסרים as 'reproofs' (from הוכחה context in Proverbs) rather than the homonym 'bonds'; the reading is contextually determined but not certain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:44.894445503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}